    {
      "parameters": {
        "jsCode": "// Stage 5: Generate personalized cold email intro — same pattern as your Generate Reply node\nconst lead = $input.first().json;\n\nconst GROQ_API_KEY = 'YOUR_GROQ_API_KEY_HERE';\n\nconst prompt = `You are an expert cold email copywriter for a home remodeling SaaS product.\nWrite a personalized cold email opener for this specific business.\n\nCompany: ${lead.company_name}\nBusiness type: ${lead.business_type || 'home remodeling company'}\nLocation: ${lead.city || ''}, ${lead.state || ''}\nKey signals about them: ${lead.key_signals || ''}\nWebsite summary: ${(lead.website_text || '').substring(0, 500)}\n\nWrite TWO things and return as JSON:\n1. subject_line: A compelling, specific email subject (under 60 chars, no clickbait)\n2. email_intro: First 2-3 sentences of the email body. Must:\n   - Reference something specific about their business (not generic)\n   - Mention a pain point home remodelers face (chasing bad leads, slow follow-up)\n   - Feel human, not like a template\n   - Max 60 words\n\nReturn ONLY valid JSON:\n{\n  \"subject_line\": \"...\",\n  \"email_intro\": \"...\"\n}`;\n\nconst response = await this.helpers.httpRequest({\n  method: 'POST',\n  url: 'https://api.groq.com/openai/v1/chat/completions',\n  headers: {\n    'Authorization': `Bearer ${GROQ_API_KEY}`,\n    'Content-Type': 'application/json'\n  },\n  body: {\n    model: 'llama-3.3-70b-versatile',\n    messages: [{ role: 'user', content: prompt }],\n    temperature: 0.7,\n    response_format: { type: 'json_object' }\n  },\n  json: true\n});\n\nlet parsed;\ntry {\n  parsed = JSON.parse(response.choices[0].message.content);\n} catch (e) {\n  parsed = {\n    subject_line: `Quick question for ${lead.company_name}`,\n    email_intro: `Hi, I came across ${lead.company_name} and wanted to reach out about how we help remodelers get better leads.`\n  };\n}\n\nreturn {\n  json: {\n    ...lead,\n    subject_line: parsed.subject_line || '',\n    email_intro: parsed.email_intro || '',\n    email_generated_at: new Date().toISOString()\n  }\n};"
      },
